today hundreds of cyclists came out to  honor the five lives lost in a horrific  crash last year the memorial bicycle  ride was held to bring awareness and  encourage safety on the roads victoria  saha spoke with those who were  courageous enough to continue riding  a goal every single rider here wants to  accomplish ghost bikes are placed at the  scene of where a bicyclist lost their  life tragically because of a driver put  the phone down  you know not drive impaired and just  really be courteous to other road users  on saturday founder of ghost bikes of  las vegas pat treachel brought a white  ghost bike with five seats honoring the  five lives lost in a grizzly crash  december 10th of 2020 it was pretty much  the 911 of the las vegas cycling  community  i personally knew all five of them a  truck driver was high on methamphetamine  when he swerved and hit the group of  cyclists on the u.s 95 near searchlight  i remember meeting just like this  fantastic morning everything was nice  michael anderson was part of that  cycling group on that fateful day i look  down the road a little bit further and i  see a pile of other riders  oh my god he says it took him about a  month to get the courage to ride again  but the trauma remained sometimes i have  to pull over on the side of the road  because i think  i am going to get smashed but that fear  didn't stop bicyclists from riding down  the strip saturday honoring those five  lives with every pedal forward victoria  saha live local now
 

